eature_054 level_002-versus-level_001 comparisons across outcome panels, null feature_063 effects on most outcomes, null or weak feature_034 and feature_060 effects on several noisy outcomes, null feature_002 effects on key noisy outcomes, and null feature_042 associations for most outcomes outside outcome_001/outcome_008. Validated failures, including H23, H26, H49, H57, H59, H196, and now H106, illustrate that several discovery signals were false-positive or non-replicating, especially in high-variance outcomes and after subgroup selection. The most informative remaining uncertainty is the feature_042-outcome_001 stronger-dependency line: main H19 is 0.0440 [0.0035, 0.0844] versus benchmark about 0.0415, with coherent positive subgroup estimates in H183, H189, and H192, but complements are weaker and there is no independent validation. If further validation is pursued, H19 is the most informative target because it is the central main-effect claim rather than a post-hoc subgroup; acceptance should require a validation interval whose lower bound is at or above about 0.0415 in the claimed direction, preferably with discovery coherence. If H19 validation fails, the feature_042-outcome_001 line should be closed as unsupported. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations; none establish causality or generalizability.",
